			"notes": "## Changes\n\n- Added Minecraft 26.3 support, including its expanded entity-collision query during step-up movement and chunk-ticking-dependent entity pushability.\n- Added a Minecraft 26.1 build. Minecraft 26.2 retains the alpha.7 collision behavior and now includes the shared exception-handling improvements.\n- Minecraft 26.1, 26.2, and 26.3 now retain native exception details in Java error reports, propagate fatal errors without ordinary exception wrapping, and skip catch-based recovery cleanup for fatal errors.\n- Added regression coverage for elevated hard colliders, ticking-state changes, and native error propagation."
		}
